-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.3 (2026-11-01)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * ORDER 350: a failed update-grub at configure and at grub2-common's trigger is run, said and kept by the
    edition's one engine, sparky-stereo-problems, with its output, until update-grub works again, and shown by
    its session notifier; the messages, word for word, are built into journal catalogs (LOCAL3, their title,
    in the nine languages). At remove and purge the package's catalogs are gone, so its own nine-language
    diagnostic, the log in /var/log and dpkg's failed state tell, as before; its problems go at its removal
  * Stop on gettext errors and require all edition language catalogues
  * Fail configuration and removal when update-grub fails; say and keep its error in all nine languages
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.2 (2026-10-30)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Removal too (ORDER 298c): on remove and purge, once Debian's catalogues are back, GRUB's menu is written
    again (update-grub, where /boot/grub/grub.cfg exists, under the same guard), so it says Debian's words at
    once instead of keeping the merged translations until the next update-grub
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2026-10-30)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * GRUB's menu is written again (update-grub) right after the messages are merged, at install and whenever
    grub2-common updates its catalogues (ORDER 298b): the translated entries reach the menu at once instead of
    at the next update-grub of another package. Not in a live session, a chroot or a container, as
    sparky-stereo-boot's kernel keeping; only where /boot/grub/grub.cfg exists
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * First version: the messages of GRUB's shell scripts from GNU GRUB 2.14's translations, added to Debian's
    GRUB catalogues at install and whenever grub2-common updates them, so the menu grub-mkconfig writes is in
    the system's language
